<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Shoprite post-exceps earnings falls.</title>
<headline>Shoprite post-exceps earnings falls.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sixteen mo ended June 30.</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, attrib (cts)</p>
<p>    - before exceptional items  327.4  vs   201.5 *</p>
<p>    - after exceptional items   129.7  vs   201.5</p>
<p>    Pre-tax			   151.28 vs   104.94</p>
<p>    Tax				  81.66 vs     6.28</p>
<p>    Net profit			 65.05 vs    99.61</p>
<p>    Turnover		     10,183.26 vs 6,363.64</p>
<p>    Extraordinary items	  99.178  vs   nil</p>
<p>* 12 months to February 1995</p>
<p>Full name:  Shoprite Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - A capitalisation share award was made in May 1996 amounting to the equivalent of 52 cents per share. An interim dividend will be declared at the time of the next interim profit announcement.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
